  <h2>About procurement in the North West</h2>
  <p>
    The North West's economy is anchored by the western platinum belt (Rustenburg–Brits) and by extensive
    agricultural production. The province runs procurement through departments coordinated by the
    North West Provincial Treasury, alongside four district municipalities. Several provincial
    departments and municipalities have been under administration in recent years, which makes
    payment-terms diligence especially important.
  </p>

  <h2>Key procuring entities</h2>

  <h3>Provincial departments</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>North West Department of Public Works and Roads</strong> — provincial buildings, road network maintenance.</li>
    <li><strong>North West Department of Health</strong> — Klerksdorp-Tshepong, Mahikeng, and district hospitals.</li>
    <li><strong>North West Department of Education</strong> — school infrastructure, scholar transport.</li>
    <li><strong>North West Department of Agriculture and Rural Development</strong> — agri-infrastructure, fencing, water provision for farmers.</li>
    <li><strong>North West Department of Community Safety and Transport Management</strong> — fleet, scholar transport, public transport.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Municipalities</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>District municipalities: <strong>Bojanala Platinum, Dr Kenneth Kaunda, Dr Ruth Segomotsi Mompati, Ngaka Modiri Molema</strong>.</li>
    <li>Constituent locals include <strong>Rustenburg, Madibeng (Brits), Matlosana (Klerksdorp), Mahikeng, Moses Kotane</strong>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Where North West tenders are advertised</h2>
  <p>
    All provincial and municipal tenders appear on the
    <a href="https://www.etenders.gov.za" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">eTenders Publication Portal</a>.
    The North West Provincial Treasury publishes annual procurement plans.
  </p>

  <h2>What sets the North West apart</h2>
  <p>
    The <strong>platinum belt municipalities</strong> — Rustenburg, Madibeng, and Moses Kotane — have
    substantial mining-related revenue streams that drive water, sanitation, and roads tenders.
    <strong>Mining-adjacent SMME and social-labour-plan procurement</strong> is also significant: mining houses
    operating in the province have community development commitments that translate into local
    contracting opportunities, often coordinated with municipal SCM units.
  </p>

  <h2>Bidding strategy</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Diligence the procuring entity's financial standing — several North West municipalities have been under administration. Verify payment terms and budget cover before mobilising.</li>
    <li>For platinum-belt work, build relationships with Social and Labour Plan coordinators at mining houses, not only with municipal SCM.</li>
    <li>Ensure CSD profile reflects current B-BBEE level and any women-, youth-, or disability-ownership status to claim the available preference points.</li>
  </ul>
